# Projects: routing index

Active work lives here. One folder per project. Each folder contains a `<ProjectName>.md` hub file that matches the folder name.

Read [[Projects]] for the status board and `next_step` for each project.

## Project routing

When new content arrives about a project, route it to the right place inside that project's folder:

| Content type | Goes to |
|---|---|
| Status update, overview, deadline, next step | `<Project>/<Project>.md` (the hub) |
| Research, competitor analysis, references | `<Project>/research/{topic}.md` |
| Specs, requirements, briefs | `<Project>/specs/{name}.md` |
| Drafts, scripts, written content | `<Project>/drafts/{name}.md` |
| Ideas, brainstorms | `<Project>/ideas/{name}.md` |
| Working notes, scratchpad | `<Project>/notes/{name}.md` |

## Rules

- **Subdirs on the fly.** Do not pre-create empty directories. When content arrives that needs a subdir, create it and write the file.
- **Hub as index.** The `<Project>.md` hub is the entry point: status, next step, key files, log. Do not duplicate subdir content into the hub. Link to it.
- **Lifecycle.** New project = `Projects/<Name>/<Name>.md` from `_template.md`, plus a row on `Projects/Projects.md`, plus a one-line mention in the root `CLAUDE.md` Active Projects section.
- **Frontmatter.** Every project hub carries `status` (`active | paused | dormant | archived`), `last_touched: YYYY-MM-DD`, `next_step: <imperative sentence>`. Status changes update both the hub and [[Projects]].
- **Naming.** Title-Case with hyphens. Filename inside the folder must match the folder name.

